&lt;li&gt;Own the project lifecycle from initial discovery and business case development through to post-launch stabilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM and Sales Ops to optimize the deal lifecycle, streamlining processes from initial CRM quotes to final revenue recognition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bridge the gap between finance and technical teams by documenting detailed business requirement documents (BRD) and leading User Acceptance Testing (UAT).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all system changes comply with ASC 606 standards and internal controls in close collaboration with Revenue Accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver comprehensive change management and training programs to ensure finance and sales teams are confident in new processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in Finance Transformation, Finance Operations, Consulting, or Finance Program Management within a high-growth SaaS or technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain knowledge of Quote-to-Cash cycles, GTM strategies, and Revenue Accounting (ASC 606).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency with ERPs (e.g., NetSuite) and CRM/Billing tools such as Salesforce, CPQ, Zuora Billing, or Zuora RevPro.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing complex, cross-functional initiatives and hitting deadlines with diverse stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates curiosity about AI tools and emerging technologies, with a willingness to learn and leverage them to enhance productivity, collaboration, or decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
