&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product strategy and long-term roadmap for a meaningful scope within Asana&#39;s monetization platform, making explicit prioritization tradeoffs to maximize customer value and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shift our capabilities from siloed, long-cycle features into reusable, self-service components, patterns, and APIs that enable faster, cheaper internal innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure our billing administration, product catalogue, and incentive workflows are highly reliable, scalable, and technically robust to meet evolving business demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Engineering, Infrastructure, Finance, and Data teams to streamline revenue-critical operational workflows and unblock cross-surface complexities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define durable success metrics and indicators (such as expansion, activation, and billing retention) to validate system performance and business health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience managing complex backend systems, infrastructure, or platform products, ideally with a background in engineering or a technical transition into product management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of global payment systems, billing administration, pricing/packaging configurations, and financial data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record operating independently in highly ambiguous problem spaces, balancing deep technical debt/investments against immediate business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional ability to simplify system-level and integration-level complexity into clear, sequenced architectural bets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional communication style, with a talent for building shared understanding across deeply technical and operational business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
