&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the technical strategy and decision-making across the Enterprise team, and ensure alignment with business objectives and cross-team collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow multiple senior engineers through individual coaching and technical workshops, helping them develop skills in technical strategy, system design, and decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tackle complex technical challenges spanning multiple programs, particularly in areas like permissions architecture, compliance systems, data administration, developer ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product and Design leaders to ensure technical considerations like performance, scalability, and engineering velocity are thoughtfully integrated into product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion technical excellence and best practices across the Enterprise team, evolving principles, patterns, AI tooling usage and processes to help teams ship quickly while maintaining high standards and consumer-grade user experience quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle technical escalations involving senior leadership, facilitate resolutions for complex disagreements and technical trade-offs impacting multiple teams or long-term architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design system boundaries and ownership models empowering team autonomy while ensuring cohesive technical architecture across enterprise-focused features and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with external partners including strategic vendors, enterprise customers, and technical partners, representing Asana&#39;s technical capabilities while building valuable relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrates fluency with AI tools and emerging technologies, with a willingness to learn and leverage them to enhance productivity, collaboration, or decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software engineering experience with a strong track record of leading technical strategy in complex, multi-team environments, preferably in enterprise software or B2B SaaS (or equivalent experience in related technical leadership roles).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy mentoring and developing others, and have demonstrated success helping senior engineers grow into technical leaders and expand their scope and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in several areas of scalable system architecture, such as multi-tenancy, complex permissions systems, compliance frameworks, user and data administration, API design, or enterprise security models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in collaborative environments and have experience partnering closely with Product, Design, and Business stakeholders to balance technical and business considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You successfully navigate complex technical discussions with multiple senior stakeholders, using strong communication skills to facilitate decision-making and build consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You understand enterprise platform challenges such as complex permissions and access control systems, compliance features and requirements, user administration at scale, data governance and administration, API frameworks, or scaling consumer-grade user experiences to enterprise environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying and solving systemic technical problems impacting multiple teams, with experience in areas like technical debt management, architectural evolution, or cross-team coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You connect technical work to business impact with the ability to communicate technical strategy to non-technical leadership and understand how engineering decisions drive business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
